# node_modules is never committed. The vendored dependencies ship as a single bundle
# (scripts/vendor/bruno-libs.cjs) instead: a committed tree had a 187-character path, which
# exceeds Windows MAX_PATH once a workspace prefix is added and made `git checkout` fail
# outright, and the blanket rule below silently excluded nested node_modules from it anyway.
node_modules/

# Test output (generated during development)
tests/.tmp/

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# .NET build output. tests/fixtures/*/*.csproj are real projects, so an editor's C# tooling
# (OmniSharp) restores and builds them in the background the moment the workspace is open -
# regenerating these the instant they are deleted. Never anything to commit, and previously
# unignored: an untracked obj/ or bin/ under a fixture is not visible in `git status` as a
# problem, but check-fixture-hygiene.mjs still walks it (it scans the filesystem, not git), and
# a test that copies a fixture wholesale can catch one of these mid-write.
bin/
obj/

# check-history wordlist: never commit the real one (see scripts/history-wordlist.example.txt)
history-wordlist.txt
*.wordlist.txt
